WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
jeanette mccurdy was a popular face on  nickelodeon in the 2000s but for a  number of reasons  she's stepped back from the spotlight in  recent years here's why she's not  getting cast much anymore and what the  future has in store for her  in march 2014 three racy photos of  mccurdy were leaked online  which put the future of her nickelodeon  show sam and cat in jeopardy mccurdy  seemed to imply that the culprit behind  the leak was  nba player andre drummond whom she dated  in 2013  as she tweeted to anyone disappointed i  sent those pics to one person  you can connect the dots shocked someone  would stoop so low  i just speak with candor when people  started pointing fingers at drummond he  tweeted in response  for all the speculations about leaking  anything i have nothing to do with it  i'm focused on basketball thank you  ultimately the leaker's identity was  never definitively revealed mccurdy  later took to reddit to address the  leaked photos as well as some recent  instagram selfies as she wrote  i post to social media when i want to  and how i want to and i would whether i  was in the entertainment industry or not  i don't believe people should attack me  because their image of me is destroyed  after i post a harmless  sultry photo she added i don't believe  an actor actress should lose the rights  to be themselves in an attempt to cater  to the image that was created by a  character they played that's all  ultimately sam and cat was cancelled  after just one season  not because of mccurdy's leaked photos  but because of her rocky relationship  with nickelodeon when rumors circulated  that her co-star ariana grande was being  paid more than mccurdy grande cleared  the air on twitlonger by saying  jeanette and i agreed up front that we  would be treated equally on this show in  all regards as we should be considering  we each work just as hard as the other  on this show  fans then speculated that mccurdy and  grande didn't get along but as mccurdy  explained to e news  i just feel that ariana and i were and  are extremely close and extremely  like-minded in a lot of different ways  and then sorta as the show dissolved  everybody wanted to find some sort of  hidden meaning in our relationship  she added i think we butted heads at  times but in a very sisterly way  like she knows me so well and i know her  so well that i think it was unfortunate  that things got misconstrued  after sam and cat mccurdy moved on to a  four-part web series called what's next  for sarah which she wrote co-edited  executive produced and starred in it  premiered on vimeo on august 13  2014. taking inspiration from mccurdy's  own life she played sarah an actress  whose world begins to fall apart after a  hit show she stars on gets cancelled  many viewers speculated that a  self-absorbed character named gloriana  was based on ariana grande  partly because of a physical resemblance  mccurdy never admitted that the  character was a direct reference to her  old co-star but she did address the  subject during an interview with abc  news  so i'll ask about gloriana then oh yeah  that was definitely a character  that was heightened for comedic purposes  mccurdy further explained that there  were blogs that blew the whole thing out  of proportion and that she was just  trying to make a joke out of her own  experience  she also talked about her relationship  with grande as she revealed  we've had coffee since this web series  and everything we've talked she's  awesome and i wish her all the best and  i know that she does the same for me  another major factor in mccurdy's break  from acting was the loss of her mother  debbie in 2013.  in 1995 debbie was diagnosed with breast  cancer and initially beat it back with  treatment but 15 years later the cancer  had returned and spread as mccurdy wrote  in the wall street journal in 2011.  i can't imagine how difficult it must be  for my mother to tolerate all she has  gone through and continues to go through  the pain the worry and the battle she  wakes up every day hurting  and goes to sleep hurting even more my  mother the constant optimist and ever  vestent sprightly woman i know her to be  is caged along with this hideous beast  they call cancer  in 2015 mccarty told vulture that  instead of mourning  she worked as she put it six days after  my mom died i went back to work i  thought oh if i do this vine video or if  i do this episode if i hit every mark  then i'll be fine because i'll have  something else to focus on but really i  was just putting this huge  life-changing event on the back burner  and it was slowly causing me to unravel  to the point where i would say i got to  my lowest emotional point  throughout her career mccurdy has  suffered from eating disorders which she  opened up about in a 2019 essay in the  huffington post as she explained  my disordered eating started when i was  11. as a child actress working in  hollywood i quickly learned that  remaining physically small for my age  meant i had a better chance of booking  more roles  unfortunately i had a trusty and  dedicated companion ready to help me  with my burgeoning anorexia  my mom she added i don't hold this  against my mom at all  i don't think she could help it mom had  been hospitalized for anorexia on  several occasions when she was a  teenager and i'm not convinced she ever  overcame her disordered eating  mccurdy's anorexia would turn into binge  eating and eventually bulimia  after experiencing several come to jesus  moments such as losing a tooth and  popping blood vessels in her eyes she  finally decided that she needed help and  met an eating disorder specialist she'd  already worked with a therapist a year  and a half earlier but this time she was  committed as she wrote  the important thing was getting back on  the recovery program anytime i had a  slip so that as they say in recovery the  slip doesn't become  a slide i suggest finding something  whatever your passion is whatever your  hobby is whatever  just finding something that will satisfy  you and fulfill you after the death of  her mother mccurdy felt lost and turned  to alcohol as she explained on her  podcast empty inside in 2020  i'd be drunk in the middle of the street  in france i was supposed to do a press  junket the next day i got completely  wasted  in another episode of md inside mccurdy  discussed her struggle with  obsessive-compulsive disorder and how it  was related to her mormon upbringing  as she explained in the mormon church  they teach you about this thing called  the still small voice  you're supposed to listen for it and it  kind of guides you to do what's right  for me i confused my anxiety with the  still small voice  she added i had ocd as a kid and i'd be  like okay so my still small voice is  telling me that i need to touch this  thing  ten times before i touch this other  thing ten times so that i can then go to  the door and open this five times  because the still small voice is telling  that i need to do these things  or else my mom's going to die in her  huffington post essay about her eating  disorders mccurdy explained that she  didn't want to be a role model during  her nickelodeon days on icarly  as she put it i had become acutely aware  that i was a role model for kids which i  felt like i was supposed to find cool  but actually found upsetting my great  contribution to society was walking onto  an overlit nickelodeon set shouting  lines about fried chicken  and that's what kids were looking up to  can i have a chicken pox  you want one of my chicken packs just  one puck  yeah no mccurdy further explained  there was something about the  shallowness of my success that made me  resent it that resentment  festered providing even more fuel for my  disordered eating i actively began to  engage in anorexic behavior again  obviously not everyone has to be perfect  but mccurdy found it especially absurd  to be seen as a role model for playing  an obnoxious character on a children's  show  not to mention that this was all going  on while her mother was dying and she  was suffering from disordered eating  in december 2020 it was reported that an  icarly revival with most of the original  cast was set to stream on paramount plus  but one cast member not returning was  jeanette mccurdy eight months earlier  mccurdy told elite daily that she  doesn't look back fondly on the show  as she put it i still have complicated  feelings toward my past from my  experience with nickelodeon  it's something that i work on i'd like  to get to a place of peace with my past  that would be great  on the bright side though mccurdy was at  least happy for the time she spent with  her icarly co-workers as she noted  i would not have such an enjoyable life  if these people weren't in it  the human connections you have with  people is always what determines whether  ultimately something is a good or bad  experience  while mccurdy has mixed feelings about  her icarly days it's at least heartening  to hear about the special connections  she made during her time on the show  beginning in 2015 mccurdy starred on the  canadian sci-fi series between  it ran for two seasons and after it  wasn't renewed for a third she decided  to take a break from acting and focus on  other projects this was ultimately part  of an effort to work on something she  could truly be happy about as she told  the hollywood reporter in 2018  i never got the chance to be cast in a  project i was proud to be part of  now i have a better chance of making  things i'm proud of than getting cast in  things i'm proud of  mccurdy assembled an all-female crew as  she wrote and directed the short film  kenny which was inspired by her mother's  death  it premiered in 2018 on short of the  week a youtube channel that showcases  short films from around the world  mccurdy has also written and directed  other short films like the mccurdy's  which is based on her childhood  and strong independent women which  covers eating disorders  in 2020 mccurdy started hosting the  podcast empty inside which covers many  personal topics  such as stage parents rejection and  dating her guests have included the  likes of former american idol contestant  david archuleta filmmaker zane rubin and  comedian taylor tomlinson  mccurdy may not be acting much these  days but she appears to be doing what  makes her happy  in a february 2021 episode of empty  inside mccurdy officially announced that  she wouldn't return to acting anytime  soon as she put it i quit a few years  ago because i initially didn't want to  do it my mom put me in it when i was six  and by age 10 or 11 i was the main  financial support for my family  and it was very much just like the  pressure of my family didn't have a lot  of money and this was kind of the way  out which i actually think was helpful  in driving me to some degree of success  mccurdy also noted that acting was  difficult because of her nerves during  auditions and that she lost much of her  interest in acting after her mom died  with her death kind of died a lot of her  ideas for my life and that was  that was its own its own journey and a  difficult one for sure she also  reiterated that she feels ashamed of  many roles that she played  as she explained i resent my career in a  lot of ways i feel so unfulfilled by the  roles that i played and felt like it was  the most cheesy  embarrassing i did the shows that i was  on from like 13 to 21 and by 15 i was  already embarrassed  my friends at 15 they're not like oh  cool you're on this nickelodeon show  it was embarrassing we're sad to hear  that mccurdy has no intentions of acting  again anytime soon but we're glad that  she's now choosing to do what makes her  happy  if you or someone you know is struggling  with addiction please call the substance  abuse and mental health administration's  24 7 national helpline  at 1-800-662-help that's 1-800-662-4357

